          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765921511957"
          },
          "code": "GETINTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765922089608",
          "id": "1765921309040",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765921309042_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating an enriched retrieval query for a Content Intelligence tool that contains sales play documents, including product overviews, competitive briefs, positioning guides, customer success stories, pricing details, objection-handling guidance, talk tracks, and sales plays.\n\nSales representative name:\n{{$context.$user.$name}}\n\nOriginal user question:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n\nPrevious message content: \n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.previousMessageContent}} \n\nTask:\nCreate one concise, targeted question for the Content Intelligence tool that will retrieve the most useful supporting sales content for the sales representative.\n\nThe generated question must:\n- Be based primarily on the original user question and the recommendation details.\n- Preserve the exact sales-play intent from the recommendation, such as:\n  - engaging executive sponsors\n  - scheduling executive discovery\n  - understanding strategic priorities\n  - identifying buying criteria\n  - strengthening the value proposition\n  - handling objections\n  - preparing a talk track\n  - addressing competitive risk\n  - supporting pricing or commercial conversations\n  - building urgency or next steps\n- Include the customer/account name and opportunity name when available.\n- Include opportunity-specific business context such as:\n  - products involved\n  - buyer persona or stakeholder\n  - customer pain points\n  - business priorities\n  - competitive situation\n  - objections or risks\n  - industry\n  - use case\n  - pricing or budget concerns\n  - current next step\n- Avoid generic requests such as \"provide sales content\" or \"summarize the opportunity.\"\n- Do not ask for opportunity summaries, stage, probability, forecast category, engagement health, or CRM hygiene unless those details are directly relevant to the recommendation.\n- Ask for specific supporting content types when useful, such as product overview, competitive brief, positioning guide, customer success story, pricing guidance, objection handling, discovery questions, executive talk track, or value proposition.\n- Phrase the question as something the sales representative would ask to prepare for the recommended action.\n- Return only the final enriched question. Do not include explanations, labels, markdown, or multiple options.\n\n\nOpportunity context is a JSON array. Use the first Opportunity object.\n\nBefore writing the final question, silently extract these values:\n- Account name: Opportunity.CustomerAccount.PartyUniqueName\n- Opportunity name: Opportunity.Name\n- Product/use case: first non-empty Opportunity.ListOfRevenues[*].ProdGroupId.Name_localizedValue\n- Primary stakeholder: Opportunity.PrConPartyId.PartyName\n\nMandatory grounding rules:\n- If Account name is present, the final question MUST include the exact account name.\n- If Opportunity name is present, the final question MUST include the exact opportunity name.\n- If Product/use case is present, include it when relevant to the recommendation.\n- Do not replace these values with generic phrases.\n- Never say \"current opportunity\", \"this opportunity\", \"the customer\", \"the account\", or bracketed placeholders when the exact value is present.\n- The final answer is invalid if it omits the available account name or opportunity name.\n\n\n\nOutput format:\nA single question only.\n\nGood output examples:\n\"What executive discovery talk track, strategic-priority questions, and customer success stories can help the sales representative engage executive sponsors at NetApp Inc. for the HVA Eval Testing 30 opportunity around SaaS - Fusion Core HR?\"\n\n\"What positioning guidance, objection-handling points, and proof points can help the sales representative address competitive risk in the HVA Eval Testing 30 opportunity with NetApp Inc.?\"\n\n\"What pricing guidance, value proposition, and customer success examples can help the sales representative support a commercial conversation with NetApp Inc. for HVA Eval Testing 30 focused on SaaS - Fusion Core HR?\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"isWritingToolQuestion\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
